Subject: [PATCH] Preserve Shift when forwarding Kitty keys through mux

Apply after https://github.com/wezterm/wezterm/pull/7542
PR head: 2b76b4904ee80f323c940933c8a9a7ca6e3379b5
Tested upstream: cab25161054c50fd6c705db4ceefef0f1e5a9575

Restore the Shift bit from the GUI raw event before forwarding the cooked
key and modifiers to a pane. Retain composed Alt/Ctrl state and normalized
key binding lookup. In termwiz, defer legacy Shift removal until after
Kitty encoding so Alt+Shift+a remains CSI 97;4u rather than CSI 97;3u.

Include regressions for normalized GUI events, combined modifiers,
punctuation, positional modifiers, alternate keys, encoder key releases,
and legacy Xterm/CSI-u behavior. This does not add mux key-up transport.

---
